.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREDKIM-TESTKEY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securedkim-testkey
.Nd verify DKIM DNS key record matches local private key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar selector
.Fl d Ar domain
.Fl k Ar keyfile
.Op Fl n Ar nameserver
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
fetches the DKIM public key from DNS and verifies that it matches the
specified local private key file.
This is used to confirm that DNS records are correctly published before
enabling DKIM signing.
.Pp
The tool queries
.Ar selector Ns ._domainkey. Ns Ar domain
for a TXT record, parses the DKIM key record, extracts the public key,
and compares it against the public key derived from the local private key.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s Ar selector
DKIM selector name.
Required.
.It Fl d Ar domain
Domain name.
Required.
.It Fl k Ar keyfile
Path to the private key file to compare against.
Required.
.It Fl n Ar nameserver
DNS nameserver IP address for the lookup.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
Key matches \(em DNS public key corresponds to the local private key.
.It 1
Key mismatch or DNS lookup failure.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-testkey -s 2026 -d example.com -k /usr/local/etc/securedkim/example.key
securedkim-testkey -s 2026 -d example.com -k /path/to/key.pem -n 8.8.8.8
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-genkey 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
